alysis\n   215\u2192\n   216\u2192### Pricing (per million tokens)\n   217\u2192\n   218\u2192**Haiku 3.5:**\n   219\u2192- Base Input: $${PRICING['claude-3-5-haiku-20241022'].input.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   220\u2192- Output: $${PRICING['claude-3-5-haiku-20241022'].output.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   221\u2192- Cache Write (5m): $${PRICING['claude-3-5-haiku-20241022'].cacheWrite5m.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   222\u2192- Cache Hits: $${PRICING['claude-3-5-haiku-20241022'].cacheRead.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   223\u2192\n   224\u2192**Sonnet 4.5:**\n   225\u2192- Base Input: $${PRICING['claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929'].input.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   226\u2192- Output: $${PRICING['claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929'].output.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   227\u2192- Cache Write (5m): $${PRICING['claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929'].cacheWrite5m.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   228\u2192- Cache Hits: $${PRICING['claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929'].cacheRead.toFixed(2)}/MTok\n   229\u2192\n   230\u2192### Estimated Costs\n   231\u2192\n   232\u2192| Model | Cost |\n   233\u2192|-------|------|\n   234\u2192| Haiku | $${haikuCost.toFixed(4)} |\n   235\u2192| Sonnet | $${sonnetCost.toFixed(4)} |\n   236\u2192| **Total** | **$${(haikuCost + sonnetCost).toFixed(4)}** |\n   237\u2192\n   238\u2192---\n   239\u2192\n   240\u2192*Report generated on ${new Date().toISOString()}*\n   241\u2192`;\n   242\u2192\n   243\u2192  fs.writeFileSync(outputFile, report);\n   244\u2192  console.log(`\\n\u2705 Report written to: ${outputFile}`);\n   245\u2192\n   246\u2192  // Also display to console\n   247\u2192  console.log('\\n' + '='.repeat(70));\n   248\u2192  console.log('SUMMARY');\n   249\u2192  console.log('='.repeat(70));\n   250\u2192  console.log(`Total LLM Requests: ${stats.totalLLMRequests}`);\n   251\u2192  console.log(`Haiku Requests: ${stats.haikuRequests}`);\n   252\u2192  console.log(`Sonnet Requests: ${stats.sonnetRequests}`);\n   253\u2192  console.log(`Total Cost: $${(haikuCost + sonnetCost).toFixed(4)}`);\n   254\u2192  console.log('='.repeat(70));\n   255\u2192}\n   256\u2192\n   257\u2192analyzeData().catch(console.error);\n   258\u2192\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it looks malicious. If it does, you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer high-level questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n",
