              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Now I'll provide a comprehensive architectural analysis of this script.\n\n---\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE ARCHITECTURAL ANALYSIS\n\n### ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW\n\n**Current Pattern:** Monolithic procedural script with embedded configuration and business logic.\n\nThe script follows a simple sequential pipeline:\n1. Stream JSONL input file line-by-line\n2. Parse records and identify utilization boundaries (3 \u2192 5)\n3. Accumulate token usage statistics within those boundaries\n4. Calculate costs based on hardcoded pricing\n5. Render markdown report and console output\n\nThis is a classic **single-responsibility-but-intertwined** design where data ingestion, parsing, filtering, aggregation, calculation, and reporting all exist in tight coupling within ~260 lines.\n\n---\n\n### STRENGTHS\n\n**1. Pragmatic for Scale**\n- Uses streaming (readline) rather than loading entire file into memory, which is excellent for large JSONL files (millions of lines)\n- Avoids unnecessary object allocations through aggregate-in-place approach\n\n**2. Handles Real-World Complexity**\n- Correctly handles both streaming and non-streaming API responses\n- Graceful degradation: malformed JSON lines don't crash the process\n- Optional file parameters with sensible defaults\n\n**3. Clear Intent**\n- Domain logic is explicit: utilization ranges, token types, pricing models\n- Comments explain non-obvious parsing logic (SSE streaming format)\n- Straightforward calculation formulas are easy to audit\n\n**4. Efficient Processing**\n- Single pass through data\n- No unnecessary intermediate data structures\n- Memory footprint bounded regardless of input size\n\n---\n\n### WEAKNESSES\n\n**1. CRITICAL: Hardcoded Business Logic - VIOLATION OF SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY PRINCIPLE**\n\n**Issue:** Pricing, model identifiers, and filtering criteria are embedded as constants.\n\n```javascript\n// Tightly coupled to specific models\nif (model === 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022') { ... }\nelse if (model === 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929') { ... }\n\n// Pricing duplicated and hardcoded\nconst PRICING = { 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022': { ... } }\n```\n\n**Problems:**\n- Requires code modification to add new models\n- Pricing changes demand redeployment\n- No single source of truth for model registry\n- Makes testing difficult (cannot inject test data)\n- Violates Open/Closed Principle (not open for extension without modification)\n\n**Impact:** HIGH - This is the primary architectural limitation.\n\n---\n\n**2. SEVERE: Global Mutable State - VIOLATION OF FUNCTIONAL DESIGN PATTERNS**\n\n```javascript\nconst stats = { totalLLMRequests: 0, ... }; // Global mutable object\n// Modified throughout analyzeData()\nstats.haikuRequests++;\nstats.haikuTokens.input += inputTokens;\n```\n\n**Problems:**\n- Makes testing nearly impossible (no way to reset state between tests)\n- Difficult to parallelize processing in future (can't safely process multiple files)\n- State mutations spread across 100+ lines of logic\n- Thread-unsafe for any async refactoring\n- Makes debugging harder (state changes are implicit)\n\n**Impact:** HIGH - Blocks testability and parallelization.\n\n---\n\n**3. MAJOR: No Separation of Concerns**\n\nThe code violates multiple SOLID principles:\n\n| Concern | Location | Problem |\n|---------|----------|---------|\n| **Parsing** | Lines 57-144 | Embedded in main loop |\n| **Filtering** | Lines 63-76, 79-82 | Intertwined with parsing |\n| **Aggregation** | Lines 122-134 | Mixed with model detection |\n| **Calculation** | Lines 152-162 | Tightly bound to report generation |\n| **Formatting** | Lines 164-241 | Hardcoded template logic |\n| **I/O** | Lines 243-244 | Scattered throughout |\n\n**Consequence:** To change how reports are formatted, you must touch data aggregation code. To add a new model, you must modify the parsing logic.\n\n---\n\n**4. MAJOR: Fragile String Parsing - BRITTLE RESPONSE HANDLING**\n\n**Issue:** Multiple unsafe string/JSON parse operations with minimal validation:\n\n```javascript\n// Lines 94-109: Streaming response parsing\nif (record.responseBody.includes('event: message_delta')) {\n  const lines = record.responseBody.split('\\n');\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    if (line.startsWith('data: ') && line.includes('message_delta')) {\n      const data = JSON.parse(line.substring(6)); // Blindly substring\n      // ...\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Risks:**\n- SSE format has specific RFC, not just \"line with 'data: ' prefix\"\n- No validation that substring(6) produces valid JSON\n- Silent failures: if parsing fails, `usage` remains null (no error logged)\n- Response format evolution will break parsing silently\n\n**Better approach:** Use a proper SSE parser or validate format first.\n\n---\n\n**5. MAJOR: Inflexible Range Detection Logic**\n\n```javascript\nif (utilization === 3) {\n  inTargetRange = true;\n} else if (utilization === 5 && inTargetRange) {\n  inTargetRange = false;\n}\n```\n\n**Problems:**\n- Hardcoded boundary values (what if requirements change to 2\u21924?)\n- State machine is implicit and fragile\n- Only supports one range; adding multiple ranges requires rewrite\n- No validation that 3 precedes 5\n- Silent failure if only one boundary is found\n\n**Better approach:** Make boundaries configurable parameters, use explicit state machine.\n\n---\n\n**6. MODERATE: Testing is Nearly Impossible**\n\n**Current barriers:**\n- Global state must be reset manually\n- Can't mock file I/O\n- Can't inject test pricing data\n- Can't inject test models\n- No way to verify intermediate calculations\n- Streaming API tightly coupled to readline\n\n**Testing a scenario would require:**\n1. Creating a test JSONL file\n2. Modifying code constants\n3. Running end-to-end script\n4. Parsing markdown output to verify\n\nThis is integration testing, not unit testing.\n\n---\n\n**7. MODERATE: Error Handling is Silent**\n\n```javascript\n} catch (parseError) {\n  // Skip records with parsing issues\n}\n```\n\n**Issues:**\n- Silent failures make debugging data quality issues impossible\n- No metrics on how many records were skipped\n- No indication of which records failed and why\n- Impossible to audit data integrity\n- Could hide genuine bugs vs. malformed input\n\n**Better approach:** Log skipped records with reasons, provide summary statistics.\n\n---\n\n**8. MODERATE: Unused Configuration**\n\n```javascript\ncacheWrite1h: 1.60, // Defined but never used\ncacheWrite1h: 6.00, // Defined but never used\n```\n\n**Issues:**\n- Dead code creates confusion\n- Assumption baked in (always use 5m cache, never 1h)\n- Not configurable which cache tier to assume\n- Misleading: appears this is flexible when it's not\n\n---\n\n**9. MINOR: CLI Parameter Validation**\n\n```javascript\nconst inputFile = process.argv[2] || 'data.jsonl';\n```\n\n**Issues:**\n- No validation that file exists before attempting to stream\n- No validation that output directory is writable\n- No helpful error messages for missing files\n- No --help or usage documentation\n\n---\n\n**10. MINOR: Type Safety Issues (JavaScript)**\n\n```javascript\nstats.haikuTokens.input += inputTokens; // Could be undefined + number\nrecord.responseBody.includes('event: message_delta') // String or object?\n```\n\nWhile these are tolerable in JavaScript, they're sources of subtle bugs. No runtime type checking.\n\n---\n\n### SCALABILITY CONSIDERATIONS\n\n**Handles Well:**\n- Large files (streaming approach)\n- Millions of records (O(n) single pass, constant memory)\n\n**Breaks Down At:**\n\n1. **Multiple Files:** Cannot parallelize without refactoring (global state)\n2. **Real-time Updates:** Entire file must be reprocessed; no incremental logic\n3. **Range Adjustments:** Requires code change + rerun\n4. **Historical Analysis:** Multiple runs accumulate, no deduplication\n5. **Model Additions:** Requires code modification + redeployment\n6. **Pricing Changes:** Code must be updated; no external configuration\n7. **Report Variants:** Single output format hardcoded; adding CSV/JSON requires major refactor\n\n**Estimated Breaking Points:**\n- Can handle 100M+ lines (streaming is efficient)\n- Cannot efficiently handle > 2-3 different models (hardcoded if/else)\n- Cannot parallelize (global mutable state)\n- Cannot provide real-time insights (batch only)\n\n---\n\n### MAINTAINABILITY ASSESSMENT\n\n**Current State:** MODERATE DIFFICULTY\n\n**Easy to Modify:**\n- Report template formatting\n- Pricing values (one location, clearly marked)\n- Output file paths\n\n**Difficult to Modify:**\n- Adding a new model (requires multiple code locations)\n- Changing boundary detection (implicit state machine)\n- Changing what gets reported (tightly bound to calculation)\n- Adding new token type tracking\n- Supporting multiple ranges in single run\n- Adding CSV or JSON output formats\n\n**Estimated Modification Time:**\n- Bug fix: 15-30 minutes (locate, fix, test)\n- Add model: 1-2 hours (must find all hardcoded references)\n- Add output format: 2-3 hours (requires partial refactor)\n- Performance optimization: 1-2 hours\n- Add filtering criteria: 1 hour\n\n**Technical Debt Accumulation:**\n- Each new model adds one if/else block (more branching)\n- Each new filter criteria adds another conditional\n- Each new output format duplicates report generation logic\n\n---\n\n### DESIGN PATTERNS\n\n**Identified Patterns:**\n\n1. **Stream Processing (GOOD)** - Lines 48-52 correctly use Node.js streaming\n2. **Accumulator Pattern (OKAY)** - Aggregating stats via += is functional but global\n3. **Template Literal Reporting (OKAY)** - Works but unmaintainable at scale\n\n**Missing Patterns:**\n\n1. **Strategy Pattern** - No abstraction for different output formats\n2. **Factory Pattern** - No way to create different model configurations\n3. **Repository Pattern** - No abstraction for file I/O\n4. **Dependency Injection** - Configuration is hardcoded\n5. **Builder Pattern** - Report generation is monolithic function\n6. **State Machine Pattern** - Range detection is implicit flags\n\n---\n\n### SEPARATION OF CONCERNS - DETAILED BREAKDOWN\n\n**Current:** Everything mixed together\n\n**Should Be Separated:**\n\n```\n1. CONFIG LAYER\n   - Model definitions\n   - Pricing tables\n   - Boundary values\n   - Output paths\n\n2. DATA ACCESS LAYER\n   - File streaming\n   - Line parsing\n   - JSON parsing\n\n3. DOMAIN LAYER\n   - Utilization range detection\n   - Token aggregation\n   - Cost calculation\n\n4. REPORTING LAYER\n   - Markdown generation\n   - Console output\n   - Data formatting\n\n5. ORCHESTRATION LAYER\n   - Coordinate above layers\n   - Handle errors\n   - Manage lifecycle\n```\n\n**Current Code:** All 5 layers merged into `analyzeData()` and `writeReport()`.\n\n---\n\n### ERROR HANDLING - ROBUSTNESS ASSESSMENT\n\n**Current Coverage:**\n\n| Error Type | Handling | Quality |\n|------------|----------|---------|\n| Malformed JSON | try/catch silent skip | POOR - no logging |\n| Missing fields | Default to 0 | OKAY - but unclear intent |\n| Missing files | Crash (no validation) | POOR |\n| Invalid config | No validation | POOR |\n| Streaming errors | None | POOR |\n| Report write failure | Can crash silently | MODERATE |\n\n**Specific Issues:**\n\n```javascript\n// Line 64: Can crash if responseBody isn't JSON\nconst response = JSON.parse(record.responseBody);\nconst utilization = response.seven_day?.utilization; // Optional chaining helps\n\n// Line 87: No check if requestBody exists before parsing\nconst requestBody = JSON.parse(record.requestBody);\n\n// Line 112: Non-streaming path will crash if responseBody isn't JSON\nconst response = JSON.parse(record.responseBody);\n\n// Line 243: File write errors silently ignored\nfs.writeFileSync(outputFile, report); // Can throw, caught only at top level\n```\n\n**Recommended:** Explicit validation, logging of skipped records, summary statistics.\n\n---\n\n### SPECIFIC ARCHITECTURAL RECOMMENDATIONS\n\n## 1. EXTRACT CONFIGURATION (P0 - Highest Priority)\n\n**Current Problem:** Pricing and models hardcoded throughout.\n\n**Recommended Solution:**\n\nCreate `[REDACTED_USERNAME_IN_PATH]/workspace/claude-instrument/config.js`:\n\n```javascript\n// config.js - Single source of truth for business logic\nconst MODELS = {\n  HAIKU: {\n    id: 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022',\n    name: 'Claude 3.5 Haiku',\n    pricing: {\n      input: 0.80,\n      output: 4.00,\n      cacheWrite5m: 1.00,\n      cacheRead: 0.08\n    }\n  },\n  SONNET: {\n    id: 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929',\n    name: 'Claude Sonnet 4.5',\n    pricing: {\n      input: 3.00,\n      output: 15.00,\n      cacheWrite5m: 3.75,\n      cacheRead: 0.30\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst BOUNDARIES = {\n  START: 3,\n  END: 5\n};\n\nmodule.exports = { MODELS, BOUNDARIES };\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Add new models without modifying parsing logic\n- External tools can read pricing from one file\n- Pricing becomes data-driven, not code-driven\n- Can load from environment or database later\n- Enables feature flags (which models to analyze)\n\n---\n\n## 2. SEPARATE DATA ACCESS LAYER (P0)\n\nCreate `[REDACTED_USERNAME_IN_PATH]/workspace/claude-instrument/parsers/jsonlReader.js`:\n\n```javascript\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst readline = require('readline');\n\nclass JsonlReader {\n  constructor(filePath) {\n    this.filePath = filePath;\n  }\n\n  async readRecords(onRecord, onError) {\n    try {\n      const fileStream = fs.createReadStream(this.filePath);\n      const rl = readline.createInterface({\n        input: fileStream,\n        crlfDelay: Infinity\n      });\n\n      for await (const line of rl) {\n        try {\n          const record = JSON.parse(line);\n          await onRecord(record);\n        } catch (parseError) {\n          onError(parseError, line);\n        }\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      throw new Error(`Failed to read file ${this.filePath}: ${err.message}`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = JsonlReader;\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Testable (inject mock readers in tests)\n- Reusable across multiple scripts\n- Error handling in one place\n- Can swap JSONL for CSV/SQL later\n- Streaming logic encapsulated\n\n---\n\n## 3. EXTRACT DOMAIN LOGIC (P0)\n\nCreate `[REDACTED_USERNAME_IN_PATH]/workspace/claude-instrument/domain/apiAnalyzer.js`:\n\n```javascript\nclass APIAnalyzer {\n  constructor(config) {\n    this.config = config;\n    this.stats = this.initializeStats();\n    this.skippedRecords = [];\n  }\n\n  initializeStats() {\n    return {\n      totalRequests: 0,\n      requests: {},\n      tokens: {},\n      utilizationRange: { start: null, end: null },\n      recordsProcessed: 0,\n      recordsSkipped: 0\n    };\n  }\n\n  processRecord(record) {\n    this.stats.recordsProcessed++;\n\n    if (this.isUtilizationBoundary(record)) {\n      this.updateUtilizationRange(record);\n    }\n\n    if (this.isLLMRequest(record)) {\n      this.processLLMRequest(record);\n    }\n  }\n\n  isUtilizationBoundary(record) {\n    // ... implementation\n  }\n\n  isLLMRequest(record) {\n    // ... implementation\n  }\n\n  processLLMRequest(record) {\n    // ... implementation\n  }\n\n  getStats() {\n    return this.stats;\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = APIAnalyzer;\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Business logic independent of I/O\n- Easy to unit test with mock data\n- Can validate calculations separately\n- State is localized to instance (not global)\n- Clear responsibilities\n\n---\n\n## 4. INTRODUCE STRATEGY PATTERN FOR RESPONSE PARSING (P1)\n\n**Current Problem:** Hardcoded if/else for streaming vs non-streaming.\n\n```javascript\n// Create abstract parser\nclass ResponseParser {\n  parse(responseBody) {\n    throw new Error('Must implement parse()');\n  }\n}\n\nclass StreamingResponseParser extends ResponseParser {\n  parse(responseBody) {\n    // SSE parsing logic\n  }\n}\n\nclass NonStreamingResponseParser extends ResponseParser {\n  parse(responseBody) {\n    // JSON parsing logic\n  }\n}\n\n// Factory\nfunction createResponseParser(responseBody) {\n  if (responseBody.includes('event: message_delta')) {\n    return new StreamingResponseParser();\n  }\n  return new NonStreamingResponseParser();\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Easy to add new response formats\n- Each parser is independently testable\n- Clear single responsibility\n- Reduces complexity of main parsing logic\n\n---\n\n## 5. EXTRACT REPORT GENERATION (P1)\n\nCreate `[REDACTED_USERNAME_IN_PATH]/workspace/claude-instrument/reporting/reportGenerator.js`:\n\n```javascript\nclass ReportGenerator {\n  constructor(config) {\n    this.config = config;\n  }\n\n  generate(stats) {\n    return {\n      summary: this.generateSummary(stats),\n      markdown: this.generateMarkdown(stats),\n      json: this.generateJson(stats),\n      csv: this.generateCsv(stats)\n    };\n  }\n\n  generateMarkdown(stats) { /* ... */ }\n  generateJson(stats) { /* ... */ }\n  generateCsv(stats) { /* ... */ }\n\n  calculateCosts(stats) { /* ... */ }\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Multiple output formats without core logic changes\n- Easier to test formatting independently\n- Can version reports\n- Enables templates/customization\n- Decouples reporting from analysis\n\n---\n\n## 6. ADD PROPER ERROR HANDLING AND METRICS (P1)\n\n**Current:** Silent failures\n\n**Recommended:**\n\n```javascript\nclass AnalysisMetrics {\n  constructor() {\n    this.recordsProcessed = 0;\n    this.recordsSkipped = 0;\n    this.errors = [];\n    this.warnings = [];\n  }\n\n  recordError(lineNumber, error, context) {\n    this.errors.push({\n      lineNumber,\n      message: error.message,\n      context,\n      timestamp: new Date()\n    });\n  }\n\n  getSummary() {\n    return {\n      processed: this.recordsProcessed,\n      skipped: this.recordsSkipped,\n      errors: this.errors.length,\n      errorRate: this.recordsSkipped / this.recordsProcessed\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Visibility into data quality\n- Can identify problematic data patterns\n- Audit trail for debugging\n- Alerts if error rate exceeds threshold\n\n---\n\n## 7. MAKE BOUNDARIES CONFIGURABLE (P2)\n\n**Current:** Hardcoded `3 \u2192 5`\n\n**Recommended:**\n\n```javascript\nclass RangeDetector {\n  constructor(startValue, endValue) {\n    this.startValue = startValue;\n    this.endValue = endValue;\n    this.inRange = false;\n  }\n\n  check(utilization) {\n    if (utilization === this.startValue) {\n      this.inRange = true;\n      return { event: 'START', value: utilization };\n    }\n    if (utilization === this.endValue && this.inRange) {\n      this.inRange = false;\n      return { event: 'END', value: utilization };\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Support multiple ranges without code changes\n- Can analyze time windows differently\n- External configuration of thresholds\n- Enables A/B testing different ranges\n\n---\n\n## 8. ADD VALIDATION LAYER (P2)\n\n```javascript\nclass InputValidator {\n  static validateInputFile(filePath) {\n    if (!fs.existsSync(filePath)) {\n      throw new Error(`Input file not found: ${filePath}`);\n    }\n    if (!fs.statSync(filePath).isFile()) {\n      throw new Error(`Path is not a file: ${filePath}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  static validateOutputPath(filePath) {\n    const dir = path.dirname(filePath);\n    if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) {\n      throw new Error(`Output directory does not exist: ${dir}`);\n    }\n    // Check write permissions\n  }\n\n  static validateConfig(config) {\n    if (!config.MODELS || Object.keys(config.MODELS).length === 0) {\n      throw new Error('No models configured');\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Fast-fail on invalid input\n- Better error messages\n- Catch issues before processing begins\n\n---\n\n## 9. ADD TESTING INFRASTRUCTURE (P2)\n\nCreate `[REDACTED_USERNAME_IN_PATH]/workspace/claude-instrument/__tests__/apiAnalyzer.test.js`:\n\n```javascript\ndescribe('APIAnalyzer', () => {\n  it('should accumulate Haiku tokens correctly', () => {\n    const analyzer = new APIAnalyzer(config);\n    \n    analyzer.processRecord({\n      method: 'POST',\n      url: 'https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages?beta=true',\n      requestBody: JSON.stringify({ model: 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022' }),\n      responseBody: JSON.stringify({\n        usage: { input_tokens: 100, output_tokens: 50 }\n      })\n    });\n\n    const stats = analyzer.getStats();\n    expect(stats.tokens.haiku.input).toBe(100);\n    expect(stats.tokens.haiku.output).toBe(50);\n  });\n\n  it('should respect utilization boundaries', () => {\n    // Test boundary detection in isolation\n  });\n\n  it('should handle malformed JSON gracefully', () => {\n    // Test error handling\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Confidence in refactoring\n- Document expected behavior\n- Catch regressions early\n- Enable CI/CD validation\n\n---\n\n### REFACTORED ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM\n\n```\nINPUT LAYER\n  JsonlReader\n    reads JSONL\n    handles streaming\n\nPARSING LAYER\n  ResponseParser (Strategy)\n    StreamingResponseParser\n    NonStreamingResponseParser\n\nDOMAIN LAYER\n  APIAnalyzer\n    RangeDetector\n    TokenAccumulator\n    CostCalculator\n\nREPORTING LAYER\n  ReportGenerator\n    MarkdownFormatter\n    JsonFormatter\n    CsvFormatter\n\nSUPPORT LAYER\n  Config (models, pricing, boundaries)\n  InputValidator\n  AnalysisMetrics\n  ErrorHandler\n```\n\n**Entry Point:** Main orchestrator coordinates these layers.\n\n---\n\n### IMPLEMENTATION PRIORITY\n\n| Priority | Task | Effort | Impact | Dependencies |\n|----------|------|--------|--------|--------------|\n| P0 | Extract config (MODELS, PRICING) | 30 min | HIGH | None |\n| P0 | Extract APIAnalyzer domain class | 1 hour | HIGH | config |\n| P0 | Extract JsonlReader | 30 min | MEDIUM | None |\n| P1 | Add error metrics/logging | 45 min | HIGH | APIAnalyzer |\n| P1 | Extract response parsers (Strategy) | 45 min | MEDIUM | APIAnalyzer |\n| P1 | Extract report generation | 1 hour | MEDIUM | APIAnalyzer |\n| P2 | Make boundaries configurable | 30 min | MEDIUM | config |\n| P2 | Add input validation | 30 min | MEDIUM | None |\n| P2 | Add unit tests | 2 hours | HIGH | All above |\n\n**Estimated Total:** 6-7 hours for full refactor (can be done incrementally)\n\n---\n\n### IMMEDIATE QUICK WINS (Without Major Refactor)\n\nIf time is constrained, these changes improve the codebase significantly:\n\n**1. Extract Pricing (5 minutes)**\n```javascript\n// pricing.json\n{ \"claude-3-5-haiku-20241022\": { \"input\": 0.80, ... } }\n\n// Load in code\nconst PRICING = require('./pricing.json');\n```\n\n**2. Add Skipped Records Logging (10 minutes)**\n```javascript\nconst skipped = [];\n// In error handler:\nskipped.push({ line: count, error: parseError.message });\n// At end:\nconsole.log(`Skipped ${skipped.length} records`);\n```\n\n**3. Add File Validation (5 minutes)**\n```javascript\nif (!fs.existsSync(inputFile)) {\n  console.error(`Error: Input file not found: ${inputFile}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n```\n\n**4. Extract Model Constants (10 minutes)**\n```javascript\nconst MODELS = {\n  HAIKU: 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022',\n  SONNET: 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929'\n};\n\n// Use in code\nif (model === MODELS.HAIKU) { ... }\n```\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY TABLE\n\n| Aspect | Current | Rating | Issue |\n|--------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **Functionality** | Works correctly | \u2713 Good | None |\n| **Performance** | Efficient streaming | \u2713 Good | Handles large files |\n| **Testability** | Nearly impossible | \u2717 Critical | Global state + hardcoding |\n| **Maintainability** | Difficult | \u2717 Serious | Mixed concerns |\n| **Extensibility** | Very limited | \u2717 Serious | Hardcoded models/pricing |\n| **Error Handling** | Silent failures | \u2717 Moderate | No visibility |\n| **Code Reusability** | None | \u2717 Moderate | Monolithic |\n| **Documentation** | Adequate comments | \u2713 Good | Logic is clear |\n| **Scalability** | Good (volume) | \u2713 Good | Handles 100M+ lines |\n| **Scalability** | Poor (variety) | \u2717 Serious | Cannot parallelize |\n\n---\n\n### CONCLUSION\n\n**Current State:** A functional, performance-efficient script that works well for its current narrow use case but will become increasingly difficult to maintain and extend.\n\n**Core Problem:** Mixing configuration, parsing, aggregation, calculation, and reporting into a single procedural flow makes it brittle and resistant to change.\n\n**Recommended Approach:**\n1. Start with P0 priorities (extract config, create analyzer class)\n2. Add error metrics and logging (visibility)\n3. Incrementally refactor while maintaining functionality\n4. Add tests to prevent regressions\n5. Pursue full separation of concerns\n\n**Timeline:** A well-organized team could complete this refactor in 2-3 development days while maintaining backward compatibility and adding test coverage. Incremental improvements can be applied starting today without waiting for a complete rewrite.\n\nThe script is not \"broken\" - it just needs structure to scale beyond its current scope."
