    "content": "The software-architect agent has completed a comprehensive analysis of your `analyze.js` file. Here's the executive summary:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Architecture Overview\nThe script is a **monolithic procedural design** that efficiently processes JSONL files using streaming, but mixes configuration, parsing, business logic, and reporting into a single flow.\n\n### Critical Issues (P0 Priority)\n\n1. **Hardcoded Business Logic** - Models and pricing are embedded in code, requiring redeployment for changes\n2. **Global Mutable State** - Makes testing nearly impossible and blocks parallelization \n3. **No Separation of Concerns** - All layers (I/O, parsing, calculation, reporting) are intertwined\n\n### Strengths\n\n- \u2713 Excellent streaming approach (handles 100M+ lines efficiently)\n- \u2713 Handles both streaming and non-streaming API responses\n- \u2713 Single-pass O(n) processing with constant memory\n- \u2713 Clear domain logic with explanatory comments\n\n### Weaknesses\n\n- \u2717 Cannot add new models without code changes\n- \u2717 Silent error handling (no visibility into skipped records)\n- \u2717 Testing requires end-to-end integration tests only\n- \u2717 Cannot parallelize processing (global state)\n- \u2717 Fragile string parsing for SSE responses\n\n### Recommended Refactoring Path\n\nThe analysis provides a detailed refactoring roadmap with:\n- **Estimated effort:** 6-7 hours for complete refactor\n- **Quick wins:** 30 minutes for immediate improvements\n- **Architectural pattern recommendations** (Strategy, Factory, Repository)\n- **Code samples** for each proposed improvement\n\nThe full analysis includes specific code examples, a refactored architecture diagram, priority matrix, and implementation timeline.\n\nWould you like me to implement any of the recommended improvements, or would you prefer to discuss specific aspects of the architectural analysis?",
